# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PILOT CORPUS — language-vocab (the second of the two apps James named on #68)
#
# Read at origin/dev@8228db7. Every DEFINED behaviour cites a line in
# language-vocab's own docs/DESIGN.md; every INFERRED one cites a test method
# that exists in the repo. As with habits, the citation is the point: a reader
# can go and check, and the suite asserts every behaviour cites something.
# kit:repo jemmy8oy-northstar/language-vocab@dev
# kit:promote self
#
# ⚠️ THIS APP IS A DIFFERENT SHAPE FROM HABITS, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE RESULT.
# habits has a full backend and no frontend. vocab has NEITHER: the only route in
# the whole backend is `GET /api/status` — none of MVP 2/3/4's drill or stats
# endpoints exist — and the frontend is the untouched web-template scaffold. What
# does exist is the domain: 37 tests over PinyinGrader, PoolMath, PoolService and
# SeedLoader, and they are excellent.
#
# So do NOT read this corpus's coverage number as a verdict on the app. It is a
# picture of an app that built its hardest part first and has not wired it up,
# which is a perfectly good place to be at PR 3 of 5 — its own delivery plan says
# so (DESIGN.md#delivery-plan: PR 1 ✅, PR 2 ✅, PR 3–5 outstanding).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ DEFINED — the product as docs/DESIGN.md states it ═══
#
# Every noun below is missing from the app, because the frontend is still the
# scaffold's single Home page. The generator refuses each one and names the noun.
# That refusal IS the "defined but not built" report, and nobody maintains it.

behaviour BEH-DRILL-ZHEN "Shown a Chinese word, the learner types the English meaning"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#product-shape
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:HanziLarge
  then sees region:PinyinUnderIt
  when fills field:Answer with ?english
  then sees region:Verdict

behaviour BEH-DRILL-ENZH "Shown an English word, the learner types the pinyin"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#product-shape
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:EnglishPrompt
  when fills field:Answer with ?pinyin
  then sees region:Verdict

# The line that decides what the app is FOR. Kept as a behaviour rather than a
# contract because it is checkable at the UI: the character is on screen, and the
# answer box does not want it.
behaviour BEH-CHAR-1 "Chinese characters are always displayed and never required as input"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#product-shape
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:HanziLarge
  contract no drill direction ever requires typing a hanzi character
  contract my assumption: "always" excepts an English-to-pinyin card before it is answered, where the app hides the hanzi because it would give the pinyin away; it shows once the verdict is in (pinned by language-vocab#24)

behaviour BEH-TONE-1 "Pinyin is displayed with tone marks and accepted three ways"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A1
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:PinyinUnderIt
  contract display uses tone marks (nǐ hǎo)
  contract input accepts tone numbers (ni3 hao3), toneless (ni hao), or tone marks

behaviour BEH-TONE-2 "Tones are graded softly — right syllables with wrong tones is 'almost'"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A2
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  when fills field:Answer with ?toneless
  then sees region:Verdict
  provides region:Verdict.states = correct, almost, wrong
  contract an 'almost' shows the correct tones and makes the card repeat sooner

behaviour BEH-NORMALISE-1 "Grading forgives everything that is not the point"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A7
  priority 5
  actor learner
  contract answers are trimmed and case-folded
  contract an English answer matches ANY accepted gloss
  contract pinyin accepts `v` for `ü` and ignores spacing and apostrophes

behaviour BEH-AUDIO-1 "Every card can be heard in Mandarin"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A5
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  when activates button:PlayAudio
  contract audio is browser SpeechSynthesis with a zh-CN voice — no API key, no network call

behaviour BEH-POOL-MVP "The active pool starts at ten words and grows as they are mastered"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-3
  priority 5
  actor learner
  provides pool:Active.bootstrap = first 10 by rank
  provides pool:Active.unlockAt = 3.5
  provides pool:Active.unlockBy = 5
  contract sampling from the active pool is weighted towards weakness

behaviour BEH-STRENGTH-MVP "A word's strength moves with the answer"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A4
  priority 5
  actor learner
  provides word:Any.strength = 0..5
  contract full credit +1, a miss -1, an 'almost' leaves it unchanged

behaviour BEH-STATS-1 "The stats page shows pool size, per-word strength and accuracy over time"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-4
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Stats
  then sees region:PoolSize
  then sees region:StrengthBars
  then sees region:AccuracyOverTime

behaviour BEH-CARD-1 "The card gives instant feedback and moves on with Enter"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-5
  priority 5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  when fills field:Answer with ?answer
  then sees region:Verdict
  contract feedback is green, amber with the correct tones, or red with the answer
  contract Enter advances to the next card

behaviour BEH-SEEDDATA-1 "HSK1 is seeded from versioned data in the repo"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-1
  priority 5
  actor learner
  contract the seed is versioned JSON in-repo (hanzi, pinyin, accepted glosses, level, frequency rank)
  contract loading it twice changes nothing


# ═══ INFERRED — what the code actually asserts today ═══
